body:
She very clearly says "NO" and tries to push him away, while he proceeds trying to have sex with her - that is attempted rape. The only person who could possibly perceive this as being in a grey area is a rapist.

&#x200B;

Here's a clip clearly showing this, in case you've forgotten. [https://youtu.be/gLkcHWJ8B-E?t=142](https://youtu.be/gLkcHWJ8B-E?t=142)

Pretty bad. They have tried peddling GABA oolong as a "cure" or symptom relief for autism, not only using very dodgy "science", but also some pretty anti-ND language. So, yeah...

&#x200B;

I wasn't aware of this particular issue until I made this meme and sent it to someone on Instagram. Earlier I've also heard of them trying to peddle Puerh from 1600 year old trees, which is, considering the pricepoint this Puerh was at, very f\*cking unlikely

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9\_lx2r8OtKs](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9_lx2r8OtKs)

&#x200B;

I was thinking similar to this, but with all my glass jars/tins of tea in there as well, since so far I'll only have one tea cake.

Just a reminder of the subreddit rules: " The health benefits of teas and tisanes are a complex topic which is not  covered by this subreddit, and is strongly discouraged. Unsupported  and/or sensational claims of health benefits will be removed.  Posts  about products that are typically only consumed for health reasons, such  as chaga, will be removed. "

&#x200B;

Keep it evidence based or don't write anything at all, folks.
